Rach2 for Almurut II
192 KB RAM, 176 free
Welcome to Almurut II
a 32-bit computer and
its AI accelerator.
Type tour for a show,
ls lists the programs
$ race
race: a press of the button goes on; hold it for two seconds to end
Both sides are written by hand; plain code uses the chip without its array of dot products.
$ pilot
pilot: the burkut flies by itself; a press lets you fly, and a hold of two seconds ends the program
flight 2: 0 pillars, the end of it flown by a person
flight 3: 0 pillars, the end of it flown by a person
flight 5: 0 pillars, the end of it flown by a person
flight 8: 0 pillars, the end of it flown by a person
flight 9: 0 pillars, the end of it flown by a person
The burkut flew 10 times, and the neuron learned from 4 crashes. Its best flight passed 0 pillars.
$ guess
guess: press the button or do not in every beat; hold it for two seconds to end
In 6 rounds the chip read the person 2 times: 33 of 100. A coin would be right 50 times of 100.
$ fence
fence: a press of the button makes a new field; hold it for two seconds to end
Field 7: every sheep is inside the three lines and every wolf outside, after 240 looks at an animal.
$ scope
scope: a press of the button changes the filter; hold it for two seconds to end
The filter took 261 samples. For each one the chip multiplied the last twelve samples by the twelve numbers of the filter and added the products, all in one instruction.
$ sched
sched: a press of the button makes the neuron forget; hold it for two seconds to end
The kernel guessed about 116 turns of the programs while sched ran, and 102 guesses were right: 87 of 100. Its neuron learns from every wrong guess.
$ shapes
shapes: a press of the button shows the next shape; hold it for two seconds to end
The cube as lines: 76 pictures a second.
The cube with filled sides: 34 pictures a second.
The yurt as lines: 48 pictures a second.
The yurt with filled sides: 11 pictures a second.
The burkut as lines: 51 pictures a second.
The burkut with filled sides: 11 pictures a second.
$ flight
flight: a press of the button changes how the land is drawn; hold it for two seconds to end
The flight over solid land: 12 pictures a second.
The flight over a land of wire: 20 pictures a second.
$ film
film: a press of the button shows the next scene; hold it for two seconds to end
The film ran for 8 seconds and showed 323 pictures: 40 a second. The land is pictures that the program moves; the burkut and the yurt are models that the chip turned in space for every picture.
$ mark
mark: four kinds of work with checked answers; hold the button for two seconds to end
Mark: 644 points. The processor 243 in 8832 ms, the accelerator 299 in 8573 ms, the system 892 in 4268 ms, the screen 1145 in 2452 ms. 1000 points mean as fast as the first machine of this kind on its board.
$ exit
The first process has ended with the exit code 0
The network of the scheduler: dot4 and C gave the same sum every time
No processes are left: 0 page faults repaired, 14 pages free at the least

Goodbye! The shell
has ended and the
machine has stopped.
Reset it to restart.
